cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "5G-GTP Agentic IDS: An Agentic Intrusion Detection Architecture for the 5G User Plane"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Hernández"
    given-names: "Justo"
    email: justo.hernandez@edu.upct.es
    affiliation: "Universidad Politécnica de Cartagena (UPCT)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/<github-username>/5g-gtp-agentic-ids-tfm"
abstract: >
  Master's Thesis (TFM) research codebase comparing a rule-based agentic
  detection architecture (TEID Agent -> PDU Session Agent -> Supervisor
  Agent) against classical ML (RandomForest, XGBoost) for intrusion
  detection on the 5G-NIDD dataset, built directly from raw GTP-U pcapng
  captures rather than the dataset authors' GTP-stripped Argus/CSV export.
keywords:
  - intrusion-detection
  - 5g-security
  - gtp-u
  - agentic-ai
  - network-security
  - machine-learning
  - 5g-nidd
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-04"
